# Diagnosis — V2i drives need to advance past first-run onboarding UI

- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix-cli-254-v2i-onboarding-dance
- prior branches: fix/cli-254-v2i-theme-picker-seed (Path B, both v1 + v2
  falsified via CI runs 36333931759 and 36335689592)

## Step 0 — Reproduce
- Docker-smoke against v1.9.4 with Path B v2 seed at ~/.claude.json
- V2i drives (/onboard-repo, /launch, /riff) exit 11 → mapped to 31
- Drive.log evidence: /tmp/smoke-v2/interactive-2026-09-27T17-12-23Z/
  interactive/drive.log
- Log shows Claude renders full onboarding UI: Welcome banner,
  "Let's get started", theme picker with Dark mode pre-selected via seed,
  syntax preview screen. No REPL prompt within 90s.

## Step 1 — Is / Is Not
- IS: Real Claude v2.1.197 in Docker, blocking on the theme picker
  even with hasCompletedOnboarding=true in ~/.claude.json.
- IS NOT: Seed missing (build log confirms COPY step 11/12 landed).
- IS NOT: Wrong file path (both ~/.claude/settings.json and
  ~/.claude.json tried; latter is the correct path per docs).
- Works: fake_claude fixture (drives PASS locally).

## Step 2 — Five Whys
1. Why do drives exit 31? Expect timeout waiting for DONE pattern.
2. Why timeout on DONE? Drive matched READY spuriously (any `>` in the
   picker's ANSI stream), sent prompt into picker UI, never got DONE.
3. Why did READY match spuriously? Default pattern `READY>|>` matches
   any `>` character anywhere.
4. Why is Claude still on picker despite seed? hasCompletedOnboarding
   is read (Dark mode has ✔) but Claude Code v2.1.197 still renders
   the theme picker + preview + waits for Enter to confirm.
5. What's the actual mechanism to advance? Send Enter key(s) after
   spawn, before the drive tries to match READY.

## Step 3 — Hypothesis
Adding an "onboarding dance" to smoke-expect drive_start (opt-in via
SMOKE_DRIVE_ONBOARDING_ENTERS env var, default 0) that sends N Enter
keys with sleeps after spawn will advance Claude past the picker.
V2i entry.sh sets the env var to 2. All three per-skill drives pick
it up automatically (no per-drive edits needed).

## Falsification test
Rerun docker-smoke against the modified image. Expected outcomes:
- Success: drives exit 0. REPL reached; drive_expect READY matches
  on the actual REPL prompt; DONE matches on Claude's response.
- Partial: drives exit non-31 (e.g., 30 for expect-script-bug). Read
  drive.log to see how far the dance advanced Claude.
- Failure: drives still exit 31. Read drive.log — needs more Enters
  OR a different key OR the READY pattern still matches spuriously
  during the dance sleeps.

## Alternative explanations (Peirce)
- Alt-A: Two Enters is the right count. LIKELY per drive.log — one to
  confirm theme, second in case of trust dialog or another gate.
- Alt-B: Needs more Enters. Discriminator: drive.log content after this
  runs. Extend fixture in a follow-on if needed.
- Alt-C: Claude in Docker needs a different keystroke (e.g., `y` for
  trust dialog, or arrow keys). Falsification: drive.log will show
  which UI is stuck.
- Alt-D: Claude needs the pty to signal SIGWINCH or a specific
  terminal size. Not tried yet; consider if A-C all fail.

## Confidence
Medium. The mechanism (send Enter to advance picker) is standard for
CLI onboarding flows. Uncertainty is in how many Enters Claude v2.1.197
needs before REPL.
